From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:02:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Facebook typing, receipts, edits, deletes, rich sends
 and groups

* Facebook typing both ways, and read receipts sent

Facebook showed nobody typing, told nobody we were, and never said we
had read a chat: the prpl had no send_typing, nothing read typing from
either connection, and no receipt went when the Messaging app showed a
chat.

Typing sent: send_typing hands "typing" or "not" to Go. An encrypted
chat gets a chat presence over the whatsmeow client, a plain chat
messagix's UpdatePresenceTask, as mautrix-meta's HandleMatrixTyping
does. The thread type the task names is kept from the thread rows.

Typing received: an encrypted 1:1 chat's ChatPresence and a plain 1:1
chat's LSUpdateTypingIndicator become serv_got_typing for the chat,
through the shared bridge. Group chats have no typing in libpurple 2.
The encrypted transport is marked available once connected: WhatsApp,
which carries it, only sends typing to a user who is online.

Read receipts: the "conversation-updated" UNSEEN hook of
glue/matrix_init.c, for prpl-gometa, calls gometa_go_mark_read for a
chat the app has shown. An encrypted chat's received messages are
marked read through the whatsmeow client, one receipt per sender (a
group's names its sender); a plain chat gets one ThreadMarkReadTask up
to its newest received message, as HandleMatrixReadReceipt does.

glue/tests gets gometa_init_test for the hook and send_typing.

* Change a Facebook message edited or deleted after it was shown

An edit or a "delete for everyone" in a Facebook chat was dropped: the
encrypted path read only a message's text, and the plain one only new
messages. The message kept showing as it first came.

Hand each to the transport's edit and delete signals (bridge.go's
purple_handle_message_edit and _delete), by the id the message was
stored under: the whatsmeow message id in an encrypted chat, which an
EditMessage's or a Revoke's MessageKey names; the Facebook MessageId in
a plain chat, which LSEditMessage, LSDeleteMessage and an unsent
LSDeleteThenInsertMessage name. A plain message deleted and inserted
again in one table was replaced, not deleted, and is left alone; one
that arrives already unsent is a delete.

The per-message cache of encrypted messages is kept in memory only. An
edit or delete does not need it, as it goes by id; where the cache
knows a message's sender, a change from anyone else is dropped, and an
edit updates the text a later reply quotes. After a restart a change
to an older message goes by id unchecked.

* Send a Facebook location and contact card as Messenger's own

A location or a contact card sent from the Messaging app reached
Facebook as its text: "My location" and a maps link, or the name and
numbers. The transport hands the place and the vCard to the plugin
beside the text, as it does for WhatsApp, but gometa's send_im and
chat_send did not read them.

Pass "webos-send-location" and "webos-send-contact" to Go. In an
encrypted chat, send a location as the "extended content" location
share mautrix-meta's msgconv sends, and a card as a ConsumerApplication
ContactMessage carrying the vCard (ContactTransport), each instead of
the text. A plain chat's SendMessageTask has no location or contact
kind, so there the text goes, written as WhatsApp's plugin writes one:
"Location: <name>" and a maps link, "Contact: <name>" and each number
and address. The transport still finds its outbox row by the text the
app sent. A failed native send is shown as an error; no text goes in
its place.

What we send comes back, if at all, under the id we sent it with and is
not shown again. A contact card received in an encrypted chat, or sent
from another of our devices, was dropped; it is now kept as a .vcf and
shown as a contact chip, as WhatsApp's are.

* Send a Facebook location and contact card as text again

A location or a contact card sent to an encrypted Facebook chat went
as Messenger's own message: the "extended content" location share
mautrix-meta's msgconv sends, and a ConsumerApplication ContactMessage.
Facebook took both without an error, and the Messaging app showed them
as sent, but no Messenger app showed either, not even on the sender's
own Android phone. mautrix-meta's location says it should also upload a
map preview, and it sends no contact card at all, so neither format
came from a message Messenger itself sent.

Send both as text in an encrypted chat too, as in a plain one:
"Location: <name>" and a maps link, "Contact: <name>" and each number
and address. That text was seen to arrive. A contact card received in
an encrypted chat is still kept as a .vcf and shown as a contact chip.

* Mark an encrypted Facebook chat read on Facebook too

Reading an encrypted Facebook chat on LuneOS never showed as read in
Messenger. The whatsmeow read receipts did go: the journal on the phone
has each one, sent to the sender's Messenger JID and acked by the server.
But Messenger's own apps take a chat's read state from its Facebook
("hybrid") thread, and that thread was never told.

As mautrix-meta does since "handlematrix: mark hybrid threads as read on
Lightspeed" (mautrix/meta#474), the encrypted chat's Facebook thread now
gets a ThreadMarkReadTask too, in sync group 95, up to the chat's newest
message: its time to the end of its second when it comes in whole
seconds. That counts our own messages from another device as well, which
get no whatsmeow receipt.

The thread's Facebook key is the one LSVerifyHybridThreadExists or
LSUpdateThreadAuthorityAndMappingWithOTIDFromJID names for the chat,
else for a 1:1 chat the chat's own (the partner's fbid). An encrypted
group with no named thread gets only the whatsmeow receipts.

* Facebook own edits, deletes and mentions sent; replies and news shown

The Messaging app could not edit or delete our own Facebook messages,
mentioned nobody, showed a plain chat's reply without the message it
answers, and showed a group's news ("Anna named the group ...") as a
message from whoever acted.

Edit and delete: glue/login.c hands the transport's webos-im-send-edit
and -send-delete for a Facebook account to gometa_go_send_edit and
gometa_go_send_delete (the WhatsApp path is unchanged). A plain chat's
message (its id "mid.$...") gets an EditMessageTask or DeleteMessageTask,
an encrypted one a ConsumerApplication EditMessage or Revoke over the
whatsmeow client, its MessageKey from us (in a group, naming us as its
participant), as mautrix-meta's HandleMatrixEdit and
HandleMatrixMessageRemove send them.

Mentions: send_im and chat_send hand Go the transport's
"webos-send-mentions" too. A plain chat's SendMessageTask gets
MentionData for each "@Name" of them, the text unchanged, offsets and
lengths in UTF-16 units as Messenger counts them. An encrypted message
keeps "@Name" as text: such a group is no group in the app yet, so the
app offers no mentions there.

A plain reply keeps its quote: ReplySourceId, ReplyMessageText (else
ReplySnippet) and who wrote it go to the transport as an encrypted
reply's do.

A group's news comes as an admin message that says it in words; it is
now a system line in the chat (gometa_message_type_system), which the
transport keeps without a banner, as WhatsApp's group news is.

glue/tests gets login_gate_test for the gate, and gometa_init_test
checks the mentions extra.

* Facebook groups: members, new group, add, remove, rename, leave

The Messaging app could not see who is in a Facebook group, nor make
one, add or remove people, rename one or leave it.

Members: the handler keeps who is in each group from the thread rows
(LSAddParticipantIdToGroupThread, LSRemoveParticipantFromThread,
LSRemoveAllParticipantsForThread) and puts them, without us, on the
group's chat conversation (gometa_message_type_members) whenever they
change and when the chat is opened (gometa_go_chat_joined, from
join_chat and from a message or news line opening it). The transport's
getChatMembers reads them there.

Changes: glue/login.c hands the transport's webos-im-group-create,
-invite, -remove, -rename and -leave for a Facebook account to
gometa_go_group_* (the WhatsApp path is unchanged). Each takes only a
plain group this account knows; an encrypted group still comes as a 1:1
chat and is refused. They are messagix tasks as mautrix-meta sends
them: CreateGroupTask (the new thread from LSReplaceOptimisticThread)
then RenameThreadTask for its name, AddParticipantsTask,
RemoveParticipantTask (our own fbid to leave) and RenameThreadTask.
Facebook's refusal (LSIssueNewError) or a failed send is said in the
group as a notice. Facebook's own news of a change comes over the socket
as an admin message and is shown from there; we add a line only for a
new group or a leave whose answer has none.

A group renamed elsewhere (LSSyncUpdateThreadName) is renamed here; the
buddy-list chat is found by its thread key, so it is not added a second
time under the new name, and an open chat takes the new title.
notifyChat goes through the sink, so tests see it.

Tests: gometa_groups_test.go, and in glue/tests login_gate_test for the
group gate and gometa_init_test for join_chat.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
